{"id": "11th_tamil_rev1_q031", "schema_version": "1.0", "kind": "multiple_choice", "level": "medium", "difficulty": "medium", "exam_mappings": ["group_4", "group_2", "group_2a"], "syllabus": {"class": "11", "subject_id": "general_tamil", "term": "full_year", "unit_id": "revision_megapack_1", "lesson_id": "rev_u1_u2_supp_grammar", "chapter_id": null, "topic_id": "punarchi_e_i_ai_udambadumey", "subtopic_id": null}, "texts": {"ta": {"blocks": [{"type": "text", "content": "இலக்கணம்: நிலைமொழியின் ஈற்றில் 'இ, ஈ, ஐ' ஆகிய உயிரெழுத்துகள் நின்று வருமொழியில் உயிர் வந்தால் தோன்றும் உடம்படுமெய் எது?", "media_id": null}], "options": {"A": "வ்கரம் (வ்)", "B": "த்கரம் (த்)", "C": "ய்கரம் (ய்)", "D": "ந்கரம் (ந்)"}, "explanation": "\"இ ஈ ஐ வழி யவ்வும் ஏனை உயிர் வழி வவ்வும்\" என்ற நன்னூல் விதியின்படி 'இ, ஈ, ஐ' வந்தால் 'ய்' என்னும் உடம்படுமெய் தோன்றும் (எ.கா: மணி + அடி = மணியடி)."}, "en": {"blocks": [{"type": "text", "content": "Grammar: According to Nannool rules, when a standing word ends in 'i, ee, or ai' followed by a vowel, which glide (Udambadumey) emerges?", "media_id": null}], "options": {"A": "v (வ்)", "B": "th (த்)", "C": "y (ய்)", "D": "n (ந்)"}, "explanation": "'I, Ee, Ai vazhi yavvum' dictates that palatal semi-vowel 'y' bridges the vocalic hiatus."}}, "question_data": {"assertion": null, "reason": null, "statements": [], "matching_pairs": [], "ordered_items": [], "numeric_answer": null, "passage_reference": null, "table_reference": null, "image_reference": null}, "answer": {"correct_key": "C", "accepted_keys": ["C"], "correct_order": [], "matching_answer": [], "numeric_value": null, "explanation_key": null}, "question_settings": {"is_negative_question": false, "marks": 1.5, "negative_marks": 0.0, "allow_multiple_answers": false}, "source": {"type": "book", "book_name": "Tamil Nadu Samacheer Kalvi", "publisher": "Tamil Nadu Textbook and Educational Services Corporation", "class": "11", "term": "full_year", "edition": "2024-2025", "page": 18, "chapter": null, "section": nu