{"id": "11th_tamil_rev1_q136", "schema_version": "1.0", "kind": "multiple_choice", "level": "easy", "difficulty": "easy", "exam_mappings": ["group_4", "group_2", "group_2a"], "syllabus": {"class": "11", "subject_id": "general_tamil", "term": "full_year", "unit_id": "revision_megapack_1", "lesson_id": "rev_u3_u4_supp_grammar", "chapter_id": null, "topic_id": "viyangol_suffixes_list", "subtopic_id": null}, "texts": {"ta": {"blocks": [{"type": "text", "content": "இலக்கணம்: வாழ்த்துதல், வைதல், வேண்டல், விதித்தல் ஆகிய பொருள்களில் வரும் 'வியங்கோள் வினைமுற்று விகுதிகள்' எவை?", "media_id": null}], "options": {"A": "-அன், -ஆன்", "B": "-அள், -ஆள்", "C": "-து, -று", "D": "-க, -ய, -இய, -இயர் (எ.கா: வாழ்க, வாழிய, வாழியர்)"}, "explanation": "வியங்கோள் வினைமுற்று விகுதிகளாகக் 'க, ய, இய, இயர்' ஆகியவை அமைகின்றன (வாழ்க, வாழி, வாழிய, வாழியர்)."}, "en": {"blocks": [{"type": "text", "content": "Grammar: Which suffixes characterize the optative finite verb (Viyangol Vinaimutru) expressing benediction, mandate, or wish?", "media_id": null}], "options": {"A": "-an, -aan", "B": "-all, -aall", "C": "-thu, -tru", "D": "-ka, -ya, -iya, -iyar (e.g., Vaazhga, Vaazhiya, Vaazhiyar)"}, "explanation": "Optative suffixes in classical Tamil are -ka, -ya, -iya, and -iyar."}}, "question_data": {"assertion": null, "reason": null, "statements": [], "matching_pairs": [], "ordered_items": [], "numeric_answer": null, "passage_reference": null, "table_reference": null, "image_reference": null}, "answer": {"correct_key": "D", "accepted_keys": ["D"], "correct_order": [], "matching_answer": [], "numeric_value": null, "explanation_key": null}, "question_settings": {"is_negative_question": false, "marks": 1.5, "negative_marks": 0.0, "allow_multiple_answers": false}, "source": {"type": "book", "book_name": "Tamil Nadu Samacheer Kalvi", "publisher": "Tamil Nadu Textbook and Educational Services Corporation", "class": "11", "term": "full_year", "edition": "2024-2025", "page": 73, "chapter": null, "section": null, "re